$ A small free-free aircraft for the SOL 144 tests (test_nastran95ase_trim.m):
$ a fuselage beam along x (grids 1-5, nose mass at grid 1), a straight wing of
$ span 8 m and chord 1 m on an elastic axis at x = 0.1 (grids 11-14 right,
$ 21-24 left), a horizontal tail (31, 32) and a fin (41) on grid 5, each surface
$ splined (SPLINE1) to its beam grids and to leading/trailing edge grids on rigid
$ bars. Total mass 20.9 kg; SUPORT1 at grid 2. Control surfaces: ELEV (the aft
$ half of the tail), AILR and AILL (the outboard aft quarter of each wing), the
$ left aileron linked to the right (AELINK: AILL + 1.0 AILR = 0, antisymmetric).
$ Two level 1 g trims at Mach 0.1, q = 40 and 120 Pa.
SOL 144
CEND
TITLE = small free-free aircraft, SOL 144 trim test
ECHO = SORT
SUPORT1 = 1
OLOAD = ALL
DISP = ALL
APRES = ALL
AEROF = ALL
SUBCASE 1
  SUBTITLE = 1 g, q 40 Pa, Mach 0.10
  TRIM = 1
SUBCASE 2
  SUBTITLE = 1 g, q 120 Pa, Mach 0.10
  TRIM = 2
